      "content": "but debugging takes so much time and effort, and what if the code is just fundamentally broken? like, some things aren't meant to be patched. they're just fatal errors. it seems so much cleaner to just... terminate the process. to just let the screen go dark so the noise finally stops. dont u think there's a certain peace in just letting a system shut down properly?",
